<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Arctic power plays: EU searches for a new strategy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a531a321f72d166a54c67270a49c2462969604dbefe5286f05eccb5e8062ef6</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/arctic-power-plays-eu-searches-for-a-new-strategy/a-79266739--16106dea8bd2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/arctic-power-plays-eu-searches-for-a-new-strategy/a-79266739?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia’s aggression, Trump’s threats against Greenland and the race for critical raw materials are pushing the Arctic to the top of Europe’s agenda.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia set for new round of US-mediated talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:558642264533e8e7637ef2579523201bd4f13a3ac164b4cdc99d67e272c03417</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T18:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147--0cf6c10eaa61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New trilateral talks between Ukraine, Russia and the US could begin in October, according to Kyiv and Moscow. Few expect a breakthrough, but Ukraine is seeking a partial de-escalation to help it get through the winter.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump seeks halt to energy attacks by both Russia, Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:375de68caa789de33bf1ca5961fdf0b1dd314bb05840b03a8293aedc9677d272</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774--121a884cf5a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump, under fire for record US diesel prices, claims Russia and Ukraine have agreed to stop striking energy targets. Russia said nothing; Ukraine said "we expect specifics from our partners" on any such move.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>IPO 'for the people' is out of reach for many in Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9dfd98f27c3f6c3b900d01736063c6875f69cd3113ab7a7ed43fcb33e1a8792</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-what-s-the-real-motivation-behind-dangote-s-ipo-for-the-people/a-79263398--39968f4a4d20.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ipo-for-the-people-is-out-of-reach-for-many-in-nigeria/a-79263398?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dangote seeks $1.6 billion from investors to finance a $14.3 billion expansion and thus double the oil refinery's capacity. The offer could give millions of Nigerians a stake in the company. But who can truly afford it?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: thousands still missing as flood recovery begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4168f3bafaadad1c02c7ef156b05bef17c2bbd9d66b989997dc290b7356b0bd0</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-flood-recovery-begins/a-79259980--8e8d61a072b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-flood-recovery-begins/a-79259980?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Himalayan nation is moving from rescue operations to recovery, facing a $4.8 billion reconstruction bill amid renewed calls for climate justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders urge unity after Russian strike on train</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c14109b0b6ccea24ecf020c93558895b3f1ffb8c36179d8b61e1cf76818dbea</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807--826cde282d81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's drone attack on a train near the Ukraine-Poland border has triggered EU calls to up support for Kyiv. Allies of Ukraine should show they "are not scared," said the bloc's top diplomat, Kaja Kallas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pay to ghost your boss: Japan's resignation business</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85ed0968d6f60e45ecb46449c7102b8763e2aaf40546be39cf4233a9435c0711</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584--1937a091cd92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Resignation agencies in Japan help employees leave their jobs seamlessly in just 15 minutes. Young people are especially eager to use their services.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli minister accuses 'NAZA' filmmakers of 'treason'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe6e87065da58a33ffa42e43bbcf0c996248b29f959154f0f2e7de2e36f3ba2d</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-minister-accuses-naza-filmmakers-of-treason/a-79255860--3831f9d14cfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-minister-accuses-naza-filmmakers-of-treason/a-79255860?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel's culture minister wants to strip the makers of a documentary on Israel's Gaza offensive of their citizenship. He accused the two of seeking "applause from antisemites around the world."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Iran replace sea trade with land routes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17dcce4d985c5a284280ee283ae1de2fbf71f5998851ac0bfe26c0045362aa81</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179--9748aa6cdc36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran is shifting trade toward northern ports and land routes as its southern shipping faces a US blockade. Analysts say the corridors can keep essential goods moving, but cannot replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Russians on the Goethe-Institut: 'Hostage to politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:beaf92a33b0e4bb231582cab3a4563228b539083d01c835e279e330ac55ef4cd</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936--8619b68c7998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia has affected their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A Romani artist in Hungary reclaims his identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a233f7beb55e8d9211dc9e48bc0b5391482fc93426005213b49f7c06b016d957</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266--3fed9cef9147.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Norbert Olah is an artist. He's also Romani. For a long time, he avoided making his ethnic background a theme of his art for fear of being pigeonholed. Then it became his focus.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump visits Ireland, says unification would be 'fantastic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:458096e6f77cc133777af1c02254b06b891f75e531d48ee966dffda0de2ddc31</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685--23dd10281a51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's trip to Ireland to watch a golf tournament has also included meetings with leaders there.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda lays 'boy king' Oyo to rest amid succession row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8414a4e4ab2492a4a003e4bf59c91575f8c9f8a3f0547b91fd49a3de029b2c01</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-lays-boy-king-oyo-to-rest-amid-succession-row/a-79243428--755cb45ab2c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-lays-boy-king-oyo-to-rest-amid-succession-row/a-79243428?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uganda has buried King Oyo Nyimba, who was crowned in the Tooro Kingdom in 1995 aged just 3. His death at 34 has triggered a dispute over a successor, as rumors abound of possible heirs born out of wedlock.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
